{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan revised after the BLOCK on capability classification. Measured on 1.107.9: wrapping meta with BedrockModelProfile.from_profile moves its prompt_cache_style from none to bedrock and leaves native_structured_output False, the same capability shape as amazon.nova-pro (mistral and cohere are also bedrock style). pydantic-ai applies every bedrock_cache_* setting only when the profile flags bedrock_supports_prompt_caching/bedrock_supports_tool_caching are True (models/bedrock.py 894-895, 928, 1102-1103, 1117-1118); both are False for meta, so no cachePoint is sent. structured.native_output_stack_supported is reached only under native_structured_output (structured.py:162-163), False for meta. capabilities.py is not edited; a test pins the classification and the absence of cachePoint."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794465630518854001,"uuid":"631ba20e-a025-4712-8296-85485012cd6a"}